        "beatId": 12,
        "story": "And after everything happened, Dad's career crumbled at the same rate the wall between me and him solidified. Two years later, he retired in shame, and for seven years we were the town pariahs, living in purgatory under one roof. When I finally took the online courses for business administration, finally got an interview at Supershops, and finally moved two hours away from that town, it became obvious that my parents would leave too. There was nothing holding them there anymore. They came to Calgary, and Mom's been trying to convince me to move back in with them ever since. It always sounds innocent -- \"Save money for a house or wedding\" -- but the real tone of it all is that I'm supposed to want a house and wedding. The guilt of everything I did to them would be enough, but add to that the pressure of the life they want for me, and every conversation we have is the worst. \"We can have dinner another night, I promise, when I'm better,\" I say before thinking too hard.",
        "story_cn": "一切发生后，爸爸的事业崩溃了，我和他之间的墙也以同样的速度凝固了。两年后，他羞愧地退休了，七年来，我们都是镇上的贱民，住在同一屋檐下的炼狱里。当我终于参加了工商管理的在线课程，终于在超级商店得到了面试，最后搬到了距离那个城镇两个小时的地方时，很明显我的父母也会离开。没有什么东西能把他们留在那里了。他们来到卡尔加里，从那以后妈妈一直试图说服我搬回去和他们一起住。这听起来总是天真无邪——“为房子或婚礼存钱”——但这一切的真正基调是我应该想要房子和婚礼。我对他们所做的一切感到内疚就足够了，但再加上他们想要我过的生活的压力，我们的每一次谈话都是最糟糕的。 “我保证，等我好些了，我们可以改天再吃晚饭。”我在认真思考之前说道。",
