        "beatId": 5,
        "story": "She lived with us when she first moved from Iran. She'd watch stuff like Jersey Shore to learn English and write down the words she didn't understand. The ones my mom couldn't translate would often be my job. Spending my early teen years explaining words like \"quiff\" to an innocent older lady may have affected my development in some way. She continues: \"Have you been busy? How come you never talk in the group chat?\" \"Oh, I think I need to update my app.\" I chase the straw with my mouth. If there's some FBI guy assigned to monitoring that group chat, his life has likely lost all meaning. All day long, aunties and cousins send each other: Hello Beautiful.",
        "story_cn": "当她第一次从伊朗搬来时，她和我们住在一起。她会看《泽西海岸》之类的东西来学习英语并写下她不懂的单词。我妈妈无法翻译的内容往往是我的工作。在我十几岁的时候，我一直在向一位无辜的老太太解释“quiff”这样的词，这可能在某种程度上影响了我的发展。她接着道：“你最近很忙吗？怎么从来不在群里说话？” “哦，我想我需要更新我的应用程序。”我用嘴追逐吸管。如果有某个联邦调查局人员被指派监视该群聊，那么他的生活可能就失去了所有意义。整天，阿姨和表兄弟姐妹互相发送：你好，美丽的。",
