        "story": "If I tell him what's going on, he'll probably just tell Gregory.\" Of course Armin's right. Cliff might seem genuine, but Supershops hired him to advise about layoffs first and foremost. It's impossible to really know how sympathetic he'd be when it comes down to it. He shakes his head. \"Corporations hate this kind of shit. They feed us all this sap about being a family, but at the end of the day productivity is all that matters. No one cares what's going on in your life.\" \"I understand.\" And normally I'd completely agree with him. But my mind jumps to Rhonda, to her problems with her son.",
        "story_cn": "如果我告诉他发生了什么事，他可能只会告诉格雷戈里。”当然，阿明是对的。克里夫可能看起来很真诚，但超级商店雇佣他首先是为了就裁员提供建议。不可能真正知道他在这件事上会有多同情。他摇摇头。“公司讨厌这种狗屎。他们为我们提供了作为一个家庭的所有智慧，但归根结底，生产力才是最重要的。没有人关心你的生活发生了什么。” “我理解。” 通常我会完全同意他的观点。但我的思绪跳到了朗达，跳到了她和儿子之间的问题。",
